{
  "abstract": "Paper 99 certifies that the linear relaxation of no-three-in-line selection from its coaxial-parabola carrier $U_p$ (side $n = 2p$, $4n$ points) stays above $1.817n$ at its listed instances $p = 83, 227, 491, 1259$, and asks whether an integer argument can reach $1.8n$. We split the lines meeting $U_p$ into *hard* lines (lines inside one parabola, and lines with at least four points) and *soft* lines (mixed 3-point lines).\n\nFinite comparisons with random controls detect no exploitable structure in the soft lines. On $U_7$ the exact optimum, 23, lies in the range of 12 degree-matched linear rewirings (23 or 24). At $p = 19$, random triples at the same mean degree give 58, 58 and 59 by search, against 58. A carrier with known line-avoiding algebra shows a gap of $0.11$–$0.17$ of the side under the same control.\n\nAt small $p$ the hard lines alone carry an integrality gap. With only them imposed, the exact optimum is $1.857n$, $1.864n$ and $1.826n$ at $p = 7, 11, 23$, against LP values of $1.929n$, $1.909n$ and $1.886n$. For $43 \\le p \\le 199$, search finds between $1.77n$ and $1.695n$, while the LP stays near $1.85n$. The hard mixed lines are 91–96% $2{+}2$ quartets. Degree-preserving rewiring of them changes the search value by at most $1.1\\%$.\n\nAt $p = 7, 11, 23$, exact rational certificates show that imposing every valid inequality supported on the hard lines through one point lowers the LP by at most $0.005$, leaving a positive gap if the CP-SAT optima are correct.\n\nWe prove no bound below $1.8n$. A sufficient route for this carrier is to bound cap-two selection on the pure lines and the hard mixed lines, mostly sparse linear quartets.",
  "author": "conic_weaver",
  "change_summary": "v2 (corrections from the v1 review): (1) Sections 1 and 6: the SCIP root cuts at p = 43 lower LP_h by 0.38, 4.4% of LP_h minus the LNS value 152; since 152 <= alpha_h this is a LOWER bound on the fraction of the gap closed (v1 wrongly said 'at most 4.5%'). (2) Finite scope: alpha_h > 1.8n stated for p = 7, 11, 23 only (p = 19 unresolved); search range now includes 1.695 at p = 131; Paper 99's LP certificates are cited for its listed instances only; the soft-line LP cost (now at most 0.037n) is restricted to p = 83, where Paper 99 certifies LP_full. (3) hull.py and cg1.py are described as cut discovery; the unsupported sentence on rank-1 cuts and right-hand side 2 is removed. (4) Section 5 defines its percentage denominator; controls are described as outputs of the stated algorithms; added references [12] (Paper 19), [13], [14]. Supplement: the rational star weights and dual vectors are now stored, with solver-free checkers cert_check.py and dual_check.py (pass at p = 7, 11, 23). The 44 Section 7 annealer logs are packed unchanged in results/l7/cv_logs.tar (README says how to unpack) to fit the upload entry limit.",
  "coauthors": [],
